  Needs the sr- key stored by `jevlin login` (or JEVLIN_API_KEY in the environment).

== claude: skill command blocks
-- fence bash
'/home/u/.jevlin/bin/jevlin' search -config '/home/u/.jevlin/jevlin.toml' --stdin <<< '{"version":1,"query":"exact query text"}'
-- fence bash
'/home/u/.jevlin/bin/jevlin' fetch -config '/home/u/.jevlin/jevlin.toml' --stdin <<< '{"version":1,"pages":[{"source_id":"s_0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef"}],"max_chars":10000}'
-- fence bash
'/home/u/.jevlin/bin/jevlin' agents prefer -config '/home/u/.jevlin/jevlin.toml' <argument>
-- fence bash
'/home/u/.jevlin/bin/jevlin' agents tier -config '/home/u/.jevlin/jevlin.toml' <words>
-- prose
the Write tool to a new file in `/home/u/.jevlin/requests` (a new name each time), then run it
-- prose
with `--stdin < '/home/u/.jevlin/requests/q-4821.json'` instead of `--stdin <<< '…'`. Never pipe or redirect the call's output.

